 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional course this activity belongs to, such as the school course assigning homework. References a course entity. Independent of the content targeted by activity/scope and assigned-problem/topic-coverage; does not restrict supporting topics to this course." :db/ident :activity/course :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional calendar deadline, such as an assignment due date. Distinct from a time limit measured after starting." :db/ident :activity/due :db/valueType :db.type/instant}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional positive finite estimate of the activity's total working time, including adaptive practice. Omit when calculated directly from step estimates." :db/ident :activity/expected-seconds :db/valueType :db.type/double}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Entry point into the activity; must be a member of activity/steps. This ordinary ref adds no second ownership relationship. Application stopping rules may finish an attempt before every step is presented." :db/ident :activity/first-step :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Stable identity of the activity definition, independent of learner attempts." :db/ident :activity/id :db/unique :db.unique/identity :db/valueType :db.type/uuid}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional verified Math Academy activity-definition identifier. Captured taskId values belong on learner-task; do not substitute a topic or content ID." :db/ident :activity/math-academy-id :db/valueType :db.type/long}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional curriculum content targeted by this activity. Lessons and reviews target a topic; diagnostics may target a course, unit, module, or topic. Omit when scope is fully described by the selected content. Course affiliation belongs on activity/course; assignment problem coverage belongs on assigned-problem/topic-coverage. This ordinary ref preserves shared curriculum." :db/ident :activity/scope :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many :db/doc "Immediate steps owned by this activity. The collection is unordered; first-step and the steps' continuation links define the route. Steps inside referenced multistep content belong to that multistep instead. Validate steps and their referenced content separately." :db/ident :activity/steps :db/isComponent true :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional positive finite wall-clock limit for the whole activity, measured from the task's first start. Pausing does not extend this limit." :db/ident :activity/time-limit-seconds :db/valueType :db.type/double}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Display title of the activity." :db/ident :activity/title :db/valueType :db.type/string}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Activity-type enum selecting the application's lesson, review, assessment, diagnostic, or assignment rules. An assignment may contain one multistep problem or several problems." :db/ident :activity/type :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/doc "Requires identity, title, type, steps, and an entry point. The application checks enum values, step ownership and routing, positive finite timings, and type-specific requirements: topic scope for lessons/reviews and curriculum scope for diagnostics. Assignment deadlines are optional." :db/ident :activity/validate :db.entity/attrs [:activity/first-step :activity/id :activity/steps :activity/title :activity/type]}
 {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank}
 {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox}
 {:db/ident :answer-field.type/free}
 {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio}
 {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many :db/doc "All answer values owned by this field, including authored options, canonical or reference answers, and verbatim learner-entered blank/free responses. Each answer belongs to one field; reuse identical typed values within that field. Radio/select display authored options; blank/free display editors without the bank. Each checkbox option is a separate field owning two text values, true and false. An optional free reference, or the required canonical answer for another type, must belong to this bank. An unanswered free field may have no bank members. Preserve values referenced by task-item/responses." :db/ident :answer-field/choices :db/isComponent true :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "One canonical answer, required for radio, select, blank, and checkbox fields; optional reference answer for a free field. When present, it must belong to the field's choices bank. Free references are revealed for comparison without automatic grading. This ordinary ref does not add ownership." :db/ident :answer-field/correct :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Stable identity of a field owned by one question." :db/ident :answer-field/id :db/unique :db.unique/identity :db/valueType :db.type/uuid}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Key unique within the question, binding the field to a problem location such as x or y. A single radio field can use selection without an inline placeholder." :db/ident :answer-field/key :db/valueType :db.type/string}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Interaction type for this field: :answer-field.type/radio, /checkbox, /blank, /select, or /free. The application checks supported enum membership and type-specific interaction rules. Registering a type does not supply application rendering or evaluation." :db/ident :answer-field/type :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/doc "Requires identity, key, and type when explicitly ensured. The type-specific predicate validates owned answer values and canonical membership. Radio, select, blank, and checkbox require a nonempty bank and one canonical answer. Free permits an empty bank and no reference answer. Checkbox banks contain exactly two text answers, true and false. Writers also ensure answer/validate. Question field-key uniqueness, immutable referenced values, entered-answer reuse, and response completeness require application handling." :db/ident :answer-field/validate :db.entity/attrs [:answer-field/id :answer-field/key :answer-field/type] :db.entity/preds [course-academy.answer-field/valid?]}
 {:db/ident :answer.type/image}
 {:db/ident :answer.type/math}
 {:db/ident :answer.type/text}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional feedback associated with this answer value, such as an explanation for a radio or select option." :db/ident :answer/feedback :db/valueType :db.type/string}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Stable identity of a field-scoped answer value. Reuse this entity for repeated identical values within its field; do not share it across fields." :db/ident :answer/id :db/unique :db.unique/identity :db/valueType :db.type/uuid}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Representation: answer.type/math, answer.type/text, or answer.type/image." :db/ident :answer/type :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/doc "Requires identity, type, and a string value when explicitly ensured. The application checks supported answer types and field-scoped deduplication, keeps referenced values immutable, and may validate authored image availability. Do not reject an entered value solely because its math syntax is malformed." :db/ident :answer/validate :db.entity/attrs [:answer/id :answer/type :answer/value]}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Exact answer content: learner-entered strings are retained verbatim, including empty or malformed math input. Authored math values may use LaTeX without Markdown delimiters; text and image values hold their respective content. Evaluation and normalization are separate from storage." :db/ident :answer/value :db/valueType :db.type/string}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Question or multistep containing the problem itself. This ordinary ref preserves reusable content when the assigned-problem entity is removed." :db/ident :assigned-problem/content :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Stable identity of an externally supplied problem, independent of its placement in an assignment." :db/ident :assigned-problem/id :db/unique :db.unique/identity :db/valueType :db.type/uuid}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many :db/doc "Optional mapped topics needed for this problem. The scheduler combines these targets with the enclosing assignment's deadline and learner progress to prioritize preparation. Derive prerequisites from topic/next. Absent coverage means the problem is not yet mapped; coverage does not establish question-bank membership or award mastery." :db/ident :assigned-problem/topic-coverage :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/doc "Requires identity and content when explicitly ensured. Coverage may be added later. The application checks that content references a question or multistep and coverage references topics; validate the referenced content separately." :db/ident :assigned-problem/validate :db.entity/attrs [:assigned-problem/content :assigned-problem/id]}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many :db/doc "Courses included in this catalog group. Ordinary refs define unordered membership without owning or duplicating courses. Reverse lookup supplies a course's groups. Course/next supplies progression independently; topic/next remains the prerequisite graph. Validate referenced courses separately." :db/ident :course-group/courses :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Stable identity of this course group." :db/ident :course-group/id :db/unique :db.unique/identity :db/valueType :db.type/uuid}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Catalog group title, for example High School - Traditional or Mathematical Foundations." :db/ident :course-group/title :db/valueType :db.type/string}
 {:db/doc "Requires identity, title, and at least one course ref when explicitly ensured. Nonempty titles and reference target types require application validation." :db/ident :course-group/validate :db.entity/attrs [:course-group/courses :course-group/id :course-group/title]}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional category heading, for example Differentiation. Omit for an ungrouped outcome. This is a display grouping within the course, not a reference to a curriculum unit or module." :db/ident :course-outcome/category :db/valueType :db.type/string}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Stable identity of a learning outcome owned by one course." :db/ident :course-outcome/id :db/unique :db.unique/identity :db/valueType :db.type/uuid}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "1-based display order across all outcomes in the course, continuing across category headings. Must be positive and unique within that course, not globally unique." :db/ident :course-outcome/index :db/valueType :db.type/long}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "The course-level capability stated by one outcome bullet, stored as Markdown supporting LaTeX. Excludes the bullet marker, category heading, and shared introductory sentence." :db/ident :course-outcome/text :db/valueType :db.type/string}
 {:db/doc "Requires identity, index, and outcome text when explicitly ensured. Category is optional. Nonempty text and category labels, positive indexes, index uniqueness within the course, and ownership by exactly one course require additional validation." :db/ident :course-outcome/validate :db.entity/attrs [:course-outcome/id :course-outcome/index :course-outcome/text]}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional short course code, for example AG1 or MTH 255." :db/ident :course/code :db/valueType :db.type/string}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional Markdown description of the course's purpose and overall scope. Corresponds to the Course Description section in a course map; store the section body without its heading." :db/ident :course/description :db/valueType :db.type/string}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Stable course identity assigned by our application, independent of Math Academy's identifier." :db/ident :course/id :db/unique :db.unique/identity :db/valueType :db.type/uuid}
 {:db/doc "Requires only identity for a placeholder course when explicitly ensured. Use course/validate after filling in its required data." :db/ident :course/identity-validate :db.entity/attrs [:course/id]}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional original Math Academy course identifier, taken from course-id in DATA/Courses.csv. Omit for independently created courses." :db/ident :course/math-academy-id :db/unique :db.unique/identity :db/valueType :db.type/long}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many :db/doc "Optional direct downstream courses for curriculum navigation. Ordinary refs preserve shared courses; reverse lookup supplies preceding courses. These links present progression between topic collections. Topic/next remains the authoritative prerequisite graph; course links do not impose additional whole-course completion requirements." :db/ident :course/next :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many :db/doc "Optional owned course outcomes, defined in 2-2-course-outcome.edn. Sort by course-outcome/index for display order; each outcome may have a category heading. Writers must separately ensure course-outcome/validate on each outcome." :db/ident :course/outcomes :db/isComponent true :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional Markdown overview of what students study and how the major areas connect, including teaching progression where established. Corresponds to the Course Overview section in a course map; store the section body without its heading." :db/ident :course/overview :db/valueType :db.type/string}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional name of the school offering the course, for example Oregon State University." :db/ident :course/school :db/valueType :db.type/string}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Course title without its code, for example Algebra I or Vector Calculus II." :db/ident :course/title :db/valueType :db.type/string}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many :db/doc "Units belonging to this course. At least one is required when course/validate is explicitly ensured. These ordinary refs define unordered membership; unit/next supplies navigation between units. Topic/next supplies the underlying knowledge dependencies. Referenced units must be validated separately." :db/ident :course/units :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/doc "Requires our identity, a title, and at least one unit ref when explicitly ensured. The Math Academy identifier, course code, school, description, overview, outcomes, and next courses are optional. Nonempty titles, reference target types, outcome indexes unique within this course, and prevention of self-links and cycles require application validation." :db/ident :course/validate :db.entity/attrs [:course/id :course/title :course/units]}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Next step in the same activity after a correct answer. Omit when this outcome ends the diagnostic." :db/ident :diagnostic-probe/on-correct :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Next step in the same activity after an incorrect answer when no retry is taken. Omit when this outcome ends the diagnostic." :db/ident :diagnostic-probe/on-incorrect :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional alternate step in the same activity taken when the learner accepts a retry after a submitted incorrect answer. Use a different question on the same topic at the same difficulty, distinguishable from the ordinary incorrect continuation. The completed retry replaces the original result for frontier placement; both presentations remain in history. The application offers the available retry without a timing gate; skips receive no retry. Omit this branch on the alternate step to allow only one retry." :db/ident :diagnostic-probe/on-silly-mistake :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Next step in the same activity when the learner explicitly skips the presented question. Omit when this outcome ends the diagnostic. Unpresented questions do not take this branch." :db/ident :diagnostic-probe/on-skipped :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional explanation of which component skills the containing topic exercises and why this coverage weight was chosen." :db/ident :encompassing/rationale :db/valueType :db.type/string}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "The component topic whose skills are practiced implicitly. This ordinary ref preserves the topic when the encompassing record is deleted. Validate the referenced topic separately." :db/ident :encompassing/topic :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/doc "Requires a component topic and weight when explicitly ensured. A valid topic target, finite weight in [0,1], and relationship consistency require additional validation." :db/ident :encompassing/validate :db.entity/attrs [:encompassing/topic :encompassing/weight]}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Coverage fraction from 0 to 1 describing how much practice the containing topic provides for the component topic. Distinct from learner accuracy and final repetition credit; the engine applies performance and timing rules separately." :db/ident :encompassing/weight :db/valueType :db.type/double}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Required reference to the canonical worked example question demonstrating this KP. The target must have question/id, a problem, and a nonempty worked solution. This reference establishes its worked-example role. This ordinary ref permits content reuse without cascading deletion. Canonical-example targets cannot belong to any KP practice question pool." :db/ident :knowledge-point/canonical-example :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Stable identity of the knowledge point, independent of an individual learner's progress or question occurrences." :db/ident :knowledge-point/id :db/unique :db.unique/identity :db/valueType :db.type/uuid}
 {:db/doc "Requires only identity for a placeholder knowledge point when explicitly ensured. Use knowledge-point/validate after filling in its required data." :db/ident :knowledge-point/identity-validate :db.entity/attrs [:knowledge-point/id]}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many :db/doc "Optional references to prerequisite topics whose skills are most directly used in this KP, supporting targeted remedial reviews. Distinct from the containing topic's general prerequisites. These ordinary refs do not establish ownership; omit when no links are known." :db/ident :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional reference to a question-generator entity holding a Python script that produces new questions for this KP. The application invokes the generator when more questions are needed, validates its output, and adds accepted questions to the KP's pool." :db/ident :knowledge-point/question-generator :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many :db/doc "Required pool containing at least one ordinary gradable question associated with this KP. Any question referenced through knowledge-point/canonical-example is excluded, including examples of other KPs. Lesson practice, reviews, and assessments select appropriate items from the pool using learner history. This collection is unordered; question selection and avoidance of already-answered lesson items belong to the engine." :db/ident :knowledge-point/questions :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Name of the instructional skill or case demonstrated by the worked example, corresponding to captured example titles." :db/ident :knowledge-point/title :db/valueType :db.type/string}
 {:db/doc "Native EDB specification requiring KP identity, title, a canonical example question ref, and at least one practice question ref when explicitly ensured. Writers ensure question/validate for both examples and practice questions, along with child specifications. The application checks target types, nonempty canonical worked solutions, disjointness of all canonical targets from every practice pool, mathematical correctness, and selection rules." :db/ident :knowledge-point/validate :db.entity/attrs [:knowledge-point/canonical-example :knowledge-point/id :knowledge-point/questions :knowledge-point/title]}
 {:db/ident :learner-task.status/completed}
 {:db/ident :learner-task.status/failed}
 {:db/ident :learner-task.status/locked}
 {:db/ident :learner-task.status/paused}
 {:db/ident :learner-task.status/started}
 {:db/ident :learner-task.status/unlocked}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Shared activity definition for this learner task. Resolve its title, type, and intended scope through this reference." :db/ident :learner-task/activity :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Accumulated working seconds, calculated by summing task-item/elapsed-seconds across this task's items. The application updates this total with the item durations; it is not an independently edited value or the timed-exam deadline. Omit when durations are unknown." :db/ident :learner-task/elapsed-seconds :db/valueType :db.type/double}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Stable identity of this attempt, independent of external identifiers." :db/ident :learner-task/id :db/unique :db.unique/identity :db/valueType :db.type/uuid}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many :db/doc "Owned question, tutorial, and example presentations, linked in order through task-item/next. The reference collection itself is unordered. Repeated presentations have separate item identities." :db/ident :learner-task/items :db/isComponent true :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional Math Academy taskId. Reconcile within the learner's history; global uniqueness across learners is not established." :db/ident :learner-task/math-academy-id :db/valueType :db.type/long}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Numerical scheduling priority; higher values are served first. Eligible unfinished tasks at or above the application's threshold are required. The application calculates finite values and defines the scale and threshold." :db/ident :learner-task/priority :db/valueType :db.type/double}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Locked means not yet eligible for an engine-selected start; unlocked means engine-eligible but not started. Explicit self-directed queue selections may start a prepared locked task directly without an intermediate unlock. Preparation does not start a clock or establish mastery. Started means in progress; paused means suspended and unfinished, including a lesson route whose completed presentations retain deferred practice markers while waiting for fresh questions. Completed means finished under the activity's completion rules; failed means an explicit task-level failure condition ended the attempt. Status transaction history supplies calendar timestamps, including the first start and terminal transition. Pausing does not extend a timed exam's deadline. Question correctness is recorded by task-item/status; no separate task outcome is stored." :db/ident :learner-task/status :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/doc "Requires identity, activity, and lifecycle state. The application checks one learner association, valid content, enums, and timing; validate child records separately." :db/ident :learner-task/validate :db.entity/attrs [:learner-task/activity :learner-task/id :learner-task/status]}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional nonnegative baseline XP for this attempt, before bonuses or penalties. The displayed denominator is not a maximum." :db/ident :learner-task/xp-base :db/valueType :db.type/long}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "XP awarded for this attempt, including penalties and bonuses. May be negative or exceed xp-base. Omit when unknown." :db/ident :learner-task/xp-earned :db/valueType :db.type/long}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many :db/doc "Optional collection of learner-specific tasks, including attempts and their history. Each task references a shared activity definition and records its status, elapsed working time, and XP. Status includes completed and failed; there is no separate task outcome. Tasks are defined in 3-learner-task.edn and own the items defined in 3-learner-task.edn. Calendar timestamps and history order come from status transactions. Validate each task and its learner association separately. These ordinary refs do not establish component ownership." :db/ident :learner/activity :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many :db/doc "Assignments associated with this learner. References activities whose activity/type is activity.type/assignment." :db/ident :learner/assignments :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional course currently selected in the UI. References a shared course entity." :db/ident :learner/course :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Stable learner identity used by the FIRe engine; not a login credential." :db/ident :learner/id :db/unique :db.unique/identity :db/valueType :db.type/string}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many :db/doc "Owned, unordered collection of current progress records, one per topic. Find the learner through the reverse reference learner/_knowledge-profile. Ensure learner/validate when changing membership. Partial imports may contain only known progress facts; ensure progress/validate when writing complete operational state for the engine. Retracting the learner also retracts these records, but not their shared topics." :db/ident :learner/knowledge-profile :db/isComponent true :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "The learner's display name." :db/ident :learner/name :db/valueType :db.type/string}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional owned overall performance record, defined in 1-learner.edn. Holds accuracy and evidence mass across topics. Find its learner through learner/_performance; no duplicate learner ref is needed. Ensure performance/validate separately on each performance write. Retracting the learner also retracts this record." :db/ident :learner/performance :db/isComponent true :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many :db/doc "Unordered topics explicitly selected by the learner for self-directed study. References shared topics across courses. Adding a topic requests preparation from its existing database lesson content regardless of the selected Study mode. When learner/self-directed is true, Study serves these prepared activities even without engine prerequisite eligibility, without marking them unlocked. Ongoing attempts come first, followed by lower global topic/next layers and then higher scheduling priority within a layer. An empty queue does not fall back to engine recommendations. These ordinary refs do not establish ownership. Removing a queued topic preserves the topic and all learner history. Distinct from learner/targets, which records longer-term study destinations." :db/ident :learner/queue :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Whether Study uses the learner's explicitly selected topic queue instead of engine recommendations. Applications should treat an absent value as false." :db/ident :learner/self-directed :db/valueType :db.type/boolean}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many :db/doc "Longer-term study destinations selected by the learner, displayed with their prerequisite graph. These ordinary refs point to shared topics across courses. Immediate self-directed activities come from learner/queue. Removing a target preserves its topic and all learner history." :db/ident :learner/targets :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/doc "Learner identity and knowledge-profile ownership/uniqueness. Overall performance is optional and its child record must be separately ensured with performance/validate. This spec does not validate performance ownership or values." :db/ident :learner/validate :db.entity/attrs [:learner/id] :db.entity/preds [course-academy.progress/valid-profile?]}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Stable module identity assigned by our application, independent of Math Academy's identifier and the module's order within its unit." :db/ident :module/id :db/unique :db.unique/identity :db/valueType :db.type/uuid}
 {:db/doc "Requires only identity for a placeholder module when explicitly ensured. Use module/validate after filling in its required data." :db/ident :module/identity-validate :db.entity/attrs [:module/id]}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Optional original Math Academy module identifier, taken from module-id in DATA/Modules.csv. Omit for independently created modules." :db/ident :module/math-academy-id :db/unique :db.unique/identity :db/valueType :db.type/long}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many :db/doc "Optional direct downstream modules for curriculum navigation. Ordinary refs preserve shared modules; reverse lookup supplies preceding modules. These links present progression between topic collections. Topic/next remains the authoritative prerequisite graph; module links do not impose additional completion requirements." :db/ident :module/next :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one :db/doc "Module title, taken from module-name in DATA/Modules.csv, for example Operations on Numbers." :db/ident :module/title :db/valueType :db.type/string}
 {:db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many :db/doc "Topics belonging to this module. At least one is required when module/validate is explicitly ensured. These ordinary refs permit topic reuse across modules without cascading deletion. References define unordered membership; topic/next supplies direct downstream dependencies across the shared topic graph. Referenced topics must also ensure topic/validate." :db/ident :module/topics :db/valueType :db.type/ref}
 {:db/doc "Requires our identity, a title, and at least one topic ref when explicitly ensured. The Math Academy identifier and next modules are optional. Nonempty titles, reference target types, and prevention of self-links and cycles require application validation. Referenced topics must be validated separately." :db/ident :module/validate :db.entity/attrs [:module/id :module/title :module/topics]}
